@Timer That example uses the experimental [`rewrites()`](https://github.com/isaachinman/next-i18next-vercel/blob/master/next.config.js) function and has `express` as a [dependency](https://github.com/isaachinman/next-i18next-vercel/blob/master/package.json).  Also the `next-i18next` version used in that example is beta.

My whole idea of coming up with this example was so `react-i18next` can be directly used with `Next.js` without the need for experimental features, additional server/packages (`express`, `next-i18next`) or additional configuration apart from what's mentioned in the official [`react-i18next`](https://react.i18next.com/getting-started) docs.

Avoiding experimental features was the reason I didn't want to follow the [rosetta example](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/canary/examples/with-i18n-rosetta/next.config.js) in the first place. Would the Next.js team recommend using experimental features in production?

