Commit: c63f6b926dcc343e3863e92531d982326c843544

I think this change is breaking my site, when trying to redirect using 
Router.push({
      pathname: `path`,
      query,
    });

@SarKurd sorry for the churn on this issue, but it seems we already fixed this behavior on canary: https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/15111#issuecomment-659784213

We don't want forgetting to `return` to work, and the original issue was about improving the error message (which is done).

Sorry, and thank you again!

> Shouldn't it be more advisable to add an Apollo Client v3 example since it is now the latest stable? It would significantly decrease the complexity of imports and the number of dependencies.

@balazsorban44 
yea i totally feel you. I'd update it.  Thanks.

Following-up from over here: https://twitter.com/BrandonBloom/status/1284226469263077376

Thanks for taking an interest in my struggles.

If I understand correctly, this would allow me to specify `"module": "commonjs"` in my tsconfig.json, so that that after transpilation (such as via ts-node), there will be `require` expressions instead of `import` statements. Is that right?

What downstream impact, if any, does this have on Babel & Webpack?

Additionally, and this is a known typescript shortcoming <https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/issues/16640>, I'm not sure it helps me much, as I'll still need to use https://www.npmjs.com/package/module-alias to be able to utilize `~/project/relative/paths`.

If I understand correctly, this is a step in the right direction, but not a complete solution. I'd love an easy way to run scripts subject to the full configuration of transpilation and polyfills. Bonus points if server-side configuration is available as well.

Below is a more complete solution for my specific needs. Seems like this PR would help me eliminate the `project` option extra tsconfig file. 

### run-script.js

```js
const path = require('path');

// Parse command line.
const args = process.argv.slice(2);
if (args.length === 0) {
  console.log(
    `Usage: ${path.basename(process.argv[1])} <script-name> <args...>`,
  );
  process.exit(1);
}
const scriptName = args.shift();

// Enable TypeScript transpilation.
require('ts-node').register({
  transpileOnly: true,
  project: './tsconfig.script.json',
});

// Register module aliases.
const moduleAlias = require('module-alias');
moduleAlias.addAlias('~', __dirname);

// Load polyfills.
require('isomorphic-unfetch');

// Run main function.
const mod = require(`~/scripts/${scriptName}`);
void mod.default(...args);
```

### tsconfig.script.json

```json
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "CommonJS"
  }
}
```

